    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1115">

                <pb facs="1070" n="1058" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg1058"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/27631: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Matthews</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-01-26T23:00:00+01:00">January 26,
                            1943—11 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 26—7 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>686. For the President. My 651, January 25, 8 p.m. In his message to me No. 5,
                    January 26, 2 p.m., Ambassador Steinhardt states: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Please inform the President that I have seen Prime Minister Saraçoğlu
                            after conferring with the British Ambassador. I expect to deliver the
                            President’s message to Inönü this evening or in the morning. Saraçoğlu
                            said that for his part he welcomed the proposed meeting with Churchill
                            and would urge acceptance on Inönü.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Matthews</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
